  - Vendi Score
  - psychotherapy case formulation
  - effective number of voices
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and data for a study of the semantic dispersion of a
  sixteen-model language model ensemble on psychotherapeutic case formulation, a
  task for which no correctness criterion is available. The effective number of
  voices is the Vendi Score, computed with the reference implementation rather
  than reimplemented; the per-voice dissent contribution is original to the
  study, and decomposes the ensemble's mean pairwise dissent rather than the
  spectral index. Includes the per-run indices, the per-model dissent
  contributions and the formulations produced by the panel: 7,200 model-run
  cells planned, 7,160 formulations obtained, and 7,082 analysed after the
  validity filter. The released JSONL carries all 7,200 records, each with the
  status that places it in one of the three counts. Dual-licensed: Apache
  License 2.0 for the analysis code (src/, figures/) and Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 for the published data and documentation (data/, docs/); see
  LICENSE and LICENSE-DATA in the repository. The vignette bank is not included
  and is held in a separate restricted deposit, doi 10.5281/zenodo.21708455.
